# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `problem` and `problem_type` arguments encode an optimization problem of"
" the form\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `problem` at `problem_type` arguments ay nag-encode ng optimization "
"problem sa anyo ng\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"\\min_{(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\in D} C(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
"where\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"\\min_{(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\in D} C(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C(x_1, ... , x_n) = a + \\sum_{i} b_i x_i + \\sum_{i, j} c_{i, j} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum_{k_1, ..., k_m} g_{k_1, ..., k_m} x_{k_1} ... x_{k_m}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C(x_1, ... , x_n) = a + \\sum_{i} b_i x_i + \\sum_{i, j} c_{i, j} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum_{k_1, ..., k_m} g_{k_1, ..., k_m} x_{k_1} ... x_{k_m}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By choosing `problem_type = \"binary\"`, you specify that the cost function "
"is in `binary` format, which means that $D = \\{0,  1\\}^{n}$, as in, the "
"cost function is written in QUBO/HUBO formulation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pagpili ng `problem_type = \"binary\"`, tinutukoy ninyo na ang cost "
"function ay nasa `binary` format, na nangangahulugang $D = \\{0,  1\\}^{n}$,"
" gaya ng, ang cost function ay nakasulat sa QUBO/HUBO formulation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, by choosing `problem_type = \"spin\"`, the cost function "
"is written in Ising formulation, where $D = \\{-1, 1\\}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kabilang banda, sa pagpili ng `problem_type = \"spin\"`, ang cost "
"function ay nakasulat sa Ising formulation, kung saan ang $D = \\{-1, "
"1\\}^{n}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The coefficients of the problem should be encoded in a dictionary as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align} \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\{} \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"()\"}&: \\quad &a, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i,)\"}&: \\quad &b_i, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i, j)\"}&: \\quad &c_{i, j}, \\quad (i \\neq j) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\quad  \\vdots \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(} k_1, ..., k_m  \\texttt{)\"}&: \\quad &g_{k_1, ..., k_m}, \\quad (k_1 \\neq k_2 \\neq \\dots \\neq k_m) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\}}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga coefficients ng problema ay dapat na i-encode sa isang dictionary gaya ng sumusunod:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align} \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\{} \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"()\"}&: \\quad &a, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i,)\"}&: \\quad &b_i, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i, j)\"}&: \\quad &c_{i, j}, \\quad (i \\neq j) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\quad  \\vdots \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(} k_1, ..., k_m  \\texttt{)\"}&: \\quad &g_{k_1, ..., k_m}, \\quad (k_1 \\neq k_2 \\neq \\dots \\neq k_m) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\}}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the keys of the dictionary must be strings containing a valid "
"tuple of non-repeating integers. For binary problems, we know that:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang mga keys ng dictionary ay dapat na strings na naglalaman ng "
"valid tuple ng mga non-repeating integers. Para sa binary problems, alam "
"natin na:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x_i^2 = x_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x_i^2 = x_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for $i=j$ (since $x_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$ means $x_i \\cdot x_i = x_i$). So, in "
"your QUBO formulation, if you have both linear contributions $b_i x_i$ and "
"diagonal quadratic contributions $c_{i,i} x_i^2$, these terms must be "
"combined into a single linear coefficient:\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa $i=j$ (dahil ang $x_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$ ay nangangahulugang $x_i "
"\\cdot x_i = x_i$). Kaya, sa inyong QUBO formulation, kung mayroon kayong "
"parehong linear contributions na $b_i x_i$ at diagonal quadratic "
"contributions na $c_{i,i} x_i^2$, ang mga terms na ito ay dapat pagsamahin "
"sa isang linear coefficient:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Total linear coefficient for variable $x_i$:** $b_i + c_{i,i}$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kabuuang linear coefficient para sa variable na $x_i$:** $b_i + c_{i,i}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means:\n"
"- Linear terms like `\"(i, )\"` contain: original linear coefficient + diagonal quadratic coefficient\n"
"- Diagonal quadratic terms like `\"(i, i)\"` should **NOT** appear in the final dictionary\n"
"- Only off-diagonal quadratic terms like `\"(i, j)\"` where $i \\neq j$ should be included as separate entries\n"
msgstr ""
"Nangangahulugan ito na:\n"
"- Ang linear terms tulad ng `\"(i, )\"` ay naglalaman ng: orihinal na linear coefficient + diagonal quadratic coefficient\n"
"- Ang diagonal quadratic terms tulad ng `\"(i, i)\"` ay **HINDI** dapat lumitaw sa huling dictionary\n"
"- Ang off-diagonal quadratic terms lamang tulad ng `\"(i, j)\"` kung saan ang $i \\neq j$ ay dapat isama bilang hiwalay na entries\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example:** If your QUBO has $3x_1 + 2x_1^2 + 4x_1 x_2$, the Iskay dictionary should contain:\n"
"- `\"(0, )\"`: `5.0` (combining $3 + 2 = 5$)\n"
"- `\"(0, 1)\"`: `4.0` (off-diagonal term)\n"
msgstr ""
"**Halimbawa:** Kung ang inyong QUBO ay may $3x_1 + 2x_1^2 + 4x_1 x_2$, ang Iskay dictionary ay dapat maglaman ng:\n"
"- `\"(0, )\"`: `5.0` (pinagsasama ang $3 + 2 = 5$)\n"
"- `\"(0, 1)\"`: `4.0` (off-diagonal term)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**NOT** separate entries for `\"(0, )\"`: `3.0` and `\"(0, 0)\"`: `2.0`.\n"
msgstr ""
"**HINDI** hiwalay na entries para sa `\"(0, )\"`: `3.0` at `\"(0, 0)\"`: "
"`2.0`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the bf-DCQO algorithm {#understand-the-bf-dcqo-algorithm}"
msgstr "Unawain ang bf-DCQO algorithm {#understand-the-bf-dcqo-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we run the optimization, let's understand the sophisticated quantum "
"algorithm that powers Iskay: **bf-DCQO (bias-field digitized counterdiabatic"
" quantum optimization)** [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago natin patakbuhin ang optimization, unawain muna natin ang sopistikadong"
" quantum algorithm na nagpapalakas sa Iskay: **bf-DCQO (bias-field digitized"
" counterdiabatic quantum optimization)** [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is bf-DCQO? {#what-is-bf-dcqo}"
msgstr "Ano ang bf-DCQO? {#what-is-bf-dcqo}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"bf-DCQO is based on the time evolution of a quantum system where the problem"
" solution is encoded in the **ground state** (lowest energy state) of the "
"final quantum Hamiltonian [\\[1\\]](#references). The algorithm addresses a "
"fundamental challenge in quantum optimization:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bf-DCQO ay batay sa time evolution ng isang quantum system kung saan ang"
" solusyon sa problema ay naka-encode sa **ground state** (pinakamababang "
"energy state) ng panghuling quantum Hamiltonian [\\[1\\]](#references). "
"Tinutugunan ng algorithm ang isang pangunahing hamon sa quantum "
"optimization:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The challenge**: Traditional adiabatic quantum computing requires very "
"slow evolution to maintain ground state conditions according to the "
"adiabatic theorem. This demands increasingly deep quantum circuits as "
"problem complexity grows, leading to more gate operations and accumulated "
"errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang hamon**: Ang traditional adiabatic quantum computing ay "
"nangangailangan ng napakabagal na evolution upang mapanatili ang ground "
"state conditions ayon sa adiabatic theorem. Ito ay nangangailangan ng "
"tumataas na malalim na quantum circuits habang tumataas ang pagiging "
"kumplikado ng problema, na nagreresulta sa mas maraming gate operations at "
"accumulated errors.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The solution**: bf-DCQO uses counterdiabatic protocols to enable rapid "
"evolution while maintaining ground state fidelity, dramatically reducing "
"circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang solusyon**: Ginagamit ng bf-DCQO ang counterdiabatic protocols upang "
"paganahin ang mabilis na evolution habang pinapanatili ang ground state "
"fidelity, na lubhang nagpapababa ng circuit depth.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical framework {#mathematical-framework}"
msgstr "Mathematical framework {#mathematical-framework}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The algorithm minimizes a cost function of the form:\n"
msgstr "Pinaliit ng algorithm ang cost function sa anyo ng:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\min_{(x_1,x_2,...,x_n) \\in D} C(x_1,x_2,...,x_n)$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\min_{(x_1,x_2,...,x_n) \\in D} C(x_1,x_2,...,x_n)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where $D = \\{0,1\\}^n$ for binary variables and:\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $D = \\{0,1\\}^n$ para sa binary variables at:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$C(x) = a + \\sum_i b_i x_i + \\sum_{i,j} c_{ij} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum "
"g_{k_1,...,k_m} x_{k_1}...x_{k_m}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$C(x) = a + \\sum_i b_i x_i + \\sum_{i,j} c_{ij} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum "
"g_{k_1,...,k_m} x_{k_1}...x_{k_m}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For our Market Split problem, the cost function is:\n"
msgstr "Para sa ating Market Split problem, ang cost function ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$C(x) = ||Ax - b||^2 = x^T A^T A x - 2 b^T A x + b^T b$$\n"
msgstr "$$C(x) = ||Ax - b||^2 = x^T A^T A x - 2 b^T A x + b^T b$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The role of counterdiabatic terms {#the-role-of-counterdiabatic-terms}"
msgstr ""
"Ang papel ng counterdiabatic terms {#the-role-of-counterdiabatic-terms}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Counterdiabatic terms** are additional terms introduced into the time-"
"dependent Hamiltonian that suppress unwanted excitations during the quantum "
"evolution. Here's why they're crucial:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang **counterdiabatic terms** ay karagdagang terms na ipinakilala sa time-"
"dependent Hamiltonian na nagsusupil ng mga hindi gustong excitations sa "
"panahon ng quantum evolution. Narito kung bakit sila mahalaga:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In adiabatic quantum optimization, we evolve the system according to a time-"
"dependent Hamiltonian:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa adiabatic quantum optimization, pina-evolve natin ang system ayon sa "
"time-dependent Hamiltonian:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$H(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t}{T}\\right) H_{\\text{initial}} + \\frac{t}{T} "
"H_{\\text{problem}}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$H(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t}{T}\\right) H_{\\text{initial}} + \\frac{t}{T} "
"H_{\\text{problem}}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $H_{\\text{problem}}$ encodes our optimization problem. To maintain "
"the ground state during rapid evolution, we add counterdiabatic terms:\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $H_{\\text{problem}}$ ay nag-encode ng ating optimization "
"problem. Upang mapanatili ang ground state sa panahon ng mabilis na "
"evolution, idinadagdag natin ang counterdiabatic terms:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$H_{\\text{CD}}(t) = H(t) + H_{\\text{counter}}(t)$$\n"
msgstr "$$H_{\\text{CD}}(t) = H(t) + H_{\\text{counter}}(t)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These counterdiabatic terms do the following:\n"
"1. **Suppress unwanted transitions**: Prevent the quantum state from jumping to excited states during fast evolution\n"
"2. **Enable shorter evolution times**: Allow us to reach the final state much faster without violating adiabaticity\n"
"3. **Reduce circuit depth**: Shorter evolution leads to fewer gates and less error\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang counterdiabatic terms na ito ay gumagawa ng sumusunod:\n"
"1. **Sinusupil ang mga hindi gustong transitions**: Pinipigilan ang quantum state na tumalon sa excited states sa panahon ng mabilis na evolution\n"
"2. **Pinagagana ang mas maikling evolution times**: Binibigyang-daan tayo na maabot ang panghuling state nang mas mabilis nang hindi lumalabag sa adiabaticity\n"
"3. **Binabawasan ang circuit depth**: Ang mas maikling evolution ay humahantong sa mas kaunting gates at mas kaunting error\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The practical impact is dramatic: bf-DCQO uses up to **10 times fewer "
"entangling gates** than Digital Quantum Annealing [\\[1\\]](#references), "
"making it practical for today's noisy quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang praktikal na epekto ay kahanga-hanga: ang bf-DCQO ay gumagamit ng "
"hanggang **10 beses na mas kaunting entangling gates** kaysa Digital Quantum"
" Annealing [\\[1\\]](#references), na ginagawang praktikal para sa quantum "
"hardware ngayon na maingay.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bias-field iterative optimization {#bias-field-iterative-optimization}"
msgstr ""
"Bias-field iterative optimization {#bias-field-iterative-optimization}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unlike variational algorithms that optimize circuit parameters through many "
"iterations, bf-DCQO uses a **bias-field guided approach** that converges in "
"approximately 10 iterations [1]:\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi tulad ng variational algorithms na nag-optimize ng circuit parameters "
"sa maraming iterations, ang bf-DCQO ay gumagamit ng **bias-field guided "
"approach** na nag-converge sa humigit-kumulang 10 iterations [1]:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Iteration process:**\n"
msgstr "**Proseso ng iteration:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Initial quantum evolution**: Start with a quantum circuit implementing the"
" counterdiabatic evolution protocol\n"
msgstr ""
"**Paunang quantum evolution**: Magsimula sa quantum circuit na nag-"
"iimplement ng counterdiabatic evolution protocol\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Measurement**: Measure the quantum state to obtain a probability "
"distribution over bitstrings\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pagsukat**: Sukatin ang quantum state upang makakuha ng probability "
"distribution sa mga bitstrings\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Bias-field calculation**: Analyze the measurement statistics and calculate an optimal bias-field $h_i$ for each qubit:\n"
"$$h_i = \\text{f}(\\text{measurement statistics}, \\text{previous solutions})$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pagkalkula ng bias-field**: Suriin ang measurement statistics at kalkulahin ang optimal bias-field na $h_i$ para sa bawat qubit:\n"
"$$h_i = \\text{f}(\\text{measurement statistics}, \\text{previous solutions})$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Next iteration**: The bias-field modifies the Hamiltonian for the next iteration:\n"
"$$H_{\\text{next}} = H_{\\text{problem}} + \\sum_i h_i \\sigma_i^z$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Susunod na iteration**: Binabago ng bias-field ang Hamiltonian para sa susunod na iteration:\n"
"$$H_{\\text{next}} = H_{\\text{problem}} + \\sum_i h_i \\sigma_i^z$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   This allows starting near the previously found good solution, effectively"
" performing a form of \"quantum local search\"\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ito ay nagbibigay-daan sa pagsisimula malapit sa dati nang natagpuang "
"magandang solusyon, na epektibong gumaganap ng isang uri ng \"quantum local "
"search\"\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Convergence**: Repeat until the solution quality stabilizes or a maximum "
"number of iterations is reached\n"
msgstr ""
"**Convergence**: Ulitin hanggang ang kalidad ng solusyon ay maging stable o "
"maabot ang maximum na bilang ng iterations\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key advantage**: Each iteration provides meaningful progress toward the "
"optimal solution by incorporating information from previous measurements, "
"unlike variational methods that must explore the parameter space blindly.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pangunahing pakinabang**: Bawat iteration ay nagbibigay ng makabuluhang "
"pag-unlad tungo sa optimal solution sa pamamagitan ng pagsasama ng "
"impormasyon mula sa nakaraang measurements, hindi tulad ng variational "
"methods na kailangang suriin ang parameter space nang bulag.\n"

